From c16e7bc3cce78ed37c3d9d815f75100add6ff7af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erwin <yzddmr7@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:13:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hexagonrpcd: add a narrow sns_registry property shim

The liuqin sensor ROM opens sns_registry and invokes method 0 while consuming sns_reg_config. Its exact skel ABI uses two input buffers and one output buffer, with an eight-byte primary input holding the property-name and property-value buffer lengths. The ROM implementation refuses output buffers shorter than Android PROPERTY_VALUE_MAX (92 bytes).

Expose only the two property names present in the pinned ROM sns_reg_config and return an empty value for both. Reject every other method, property, or scalar shape and clear response storage on all application-level rejection paths. This deliberately avoids implementing a generic Android property service.

Propagate reverse-listener failures out of hexagonrpcd so a service manager can distinguish a torn-down tunnel from a successful exit. Cover the recovered ROM wire encoding, both allowlisted names, non-empty near misses, short outputs, unsupported methods, and scalar-shape deviations with a host test.

Signed-off-by: Erwin <yzddmr7@gmail.com>

